# A node's link (draft/sharing.md in ternmesh/spec): HTTPS://TERNMESH.ORG/A/ and its address in
# base32, upper-case as a QR code holds it. Every one is served by the one page, which reads the
# address out of the URL in the browser; the URL stays as it was. Paths are case-sensitive here, so
# both cases are listed.
/A/* /node/ 200
/a/* /node/ 200

# A group's join code (draft/groups.md in ternmesh/spec): HTTPS://TERNMESH.ORG/G# and the code in
# base32. The code is after the #, which no request carries, so every one is the same request for
# /G, served by the one page that reads the code in the browser.
/G /group/ 200
/g /group/ 200
